{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2y3zc4xxixebjb5qllscchtbo4cs55q5vt73vv3z4px65yb5ycea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built the MAC landing page in **03 · Workspace**: one frame named `01_Home` (1440 wide, light mode) plus a library of reusable components next to it. I checked full-page screenshots of the frame and the component sheet, and fixed what I saw: two components were collapsing in height, the hero rows were too close together, and one button style was 2px taller than the others. I didn't edit the reference pages; the only change outside the workspace is that the default Button from 02 · Components now has two instances in the page.\n\n- **File:** https://www.figma.com/design/6seBPFMbLikic24iJhnVmD/\n- **03 · Workspace page ID:** `4:2`\n- **Screen:** `01_Home` — `10:83`\n- **Component sheet:** `Components · MAC` — `5:2`\n\n**What's on the page, top to bottom:**\n1. **Header:** the MAC logo, Service / Agency / Case Study / Resources with dropdown chevrons, Contact, a notifications bell and \"Get started\".\n2. **Hero:**\n   - Headline, intro text, \"Schedule Call\" (with arrow) and \"View Case Study\".\n   - The traffic card with a three-bar rising chart, and the \"230+\" card with a progress bar and growth badge.\n   - The \"920+\" card with four avatar placeholders and \"+\", and the video placeholder with \"HOW WE WORK\" and a play button.\n3. **Trusted by:** Paywise, Campfield and Mazeline set as text.\n4. **About** section.\n5. **Case studies:** the four filters, with UI/UX Design shown as the current filter. Card 1 is in its hover state with \"See Details\" and no caption. Cards 2 and 3 show Ai Wave and App Lancer.\n6. **Testimonial:** Michael Kaizer's quote on a dark card, with the \"01/05\" pager and previous/next buttons.\n7. **FAQ:** \"More Questions\" and \"Contact Us\", and four questions. The first is expanded with its answer; the other three are collapsed.\n8. **Blog:** heading, intro text, \"See more\" and three article cards, each with \"5 min read\" and an arrow.\n9. **Call to action:** a lime banner with \"Ready to work with us?\" and \"Get Started\".\n10. **Footer:** logo, description, the four social logos, and the Navigation, Licence and Contact columns with phone, mail and map-pin icons.\n\nAll copy is taken word for word from the brief. Thumbnails, the video poster and avatars are left as image placeholders.\n\n**Design system:** the brand lime (#99EA48), ink (#010205) and Plus Jakarta Sans are used throughout. I chose the rest myself: neutral, light-green and border colours, a type scale from 13 to 68px, a 1200px content area with 120px margins, corner radii of 20/24/28/32px plus fully rounded pills, and one soft shadow style. Every icon and logo is an instance from 04 · Media. \"More Questions\" and \"See more\" use the default Button from 02 · Components, and my Button's Dark style matches it.\n\n**Components:** Button (Dark, Lime and Outline styles), Icon Button, Nav Item, Filter Tag (Default / Hover / Selected), Header, Case Study Card, FAQ Item (Collapsed / Expanded), Article Card, Traffic Chart Card, Stat Card, Projects Card, Video Block, Client Wordmarks, Testimonial, CTA Banner, Footer, and image and avatar placeholders. Each component that has states comes with Default and Hover versions.\n\n**Prototype:** the brief says there's nothing to link between screens, so there are none. I added 16 state changes inside the components instead: hovering shows the hover state on buttons, icon buttons, nav items, filters, case-study cards and article cards. Clicking a filter selects it, and clicking a FAQ question opens or closes it.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- The header has dropdown triggers but no open dropdown panels, because the brief gives no menu items for them.\n- The progress bar is set at about 74% and the chart bar heights are illustrative, since the brief gives no values.\n- The footer uses a light background 